[]Great.  Will those of us adamantly struggling through the bugs
[]and pitfalls of patchlevel 6 be able to continue our saved games?
[]How about telling us which bits to flip in the save file?

the upgrade policy on your machine should be something like:
1) build nethack pl7 to see that it compiles okay (don't install yet)
2) while there are saved games greater than, let's say 25k (compressed)
    do not install pl7. (25k ~ 10 levels on vax)
3) when condition (2) is no longer satisfied remove all saved games
    and bones and install pl7.

you can adjust the saved game limit size to taste ...
no need to go flipping bits in save files, besides, you might miss and
then Ptah knows what might happen ...

